sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Dev as Developer
    participant Hook as .git-hooks/pre-commit
    participant Pylint as pylint

    Dev->>Hook: git commit, staging some .py files
    Hook->>Hook: split staged .py into tests/ and everything else

    Note over Hook,Pylint: Two calls, because a test module gets a<br/>looser module-length cap than anything else
    Hook->>Pylint: call 1 — the staged non-test files
    Pylint-->>Hook: per-file checks, and duplicate-code within call 1
    Hook->>Pylint: call 2 — the staged test files, --max-module-lines=1250
    Pylint-->>Hook: per-file checks, and duplicate-code within call 2

    Note over Hook,Pylint: A per-file check reads one file, so it answers the same<br/>every time. duplicate-code compares files against each<br/>other, and only inside one call — so it never compares<br/>a test file with a source file.

    alt one call holds both halves of a similar pair
        Hook-->>Dev: REFUSED — R0801, naming lines the commit never touched
        Dev->>Hook: git commit --no-verify
        Note over Dev,Hook: that also drops flake8, the spelling gate,<br/>mypy and both test suites
    else neither call holds both halves
        Hook-->>Dev: committed
    end
